Here are the **4 complete methods** you need to replace in your **JournalBulkValidationService.java**.
I have standardized them so that **Product Code is always at Index 6** and the **ERRORS column is always pushed to Index 7**.
### How this solves the Error File Re-upload Bug:
Because your Java parser is strictly programmed to only read from Index 0 to Index 6, it will **completely ignore the ERRORS column** sitting at Index 7 when a user re-uploads an error file. The old errors vanish automatically, and if there are still mistakes, fresh errors get printed perfectly in a new error file!
Furthermore, the * characters in the headers are safely ignored because the parser drops the first row completely as long as it contains the word "branch".
Replace these four methods entirely in your Java backend:
